-- Issue #6991 / generalizes #7217 (Woodchipper Dagger, item 53452): every Ascension custom item
-- (item_template.entry > 200000) eligible for disenchant (Quality 2-4, class WEAPON/ARMOR,
-- RequiredDisenchantSkill <> -1) has DisenchantID = 0, so Spell::CheckCast and Spell::EffectDisEnchant
-- reject it outright regardless of the caster's Enchanting skill. Backfill each such row from the
-- nearest-ItemLevel-at-or-below stock donor (entry < 60000) sharing the same class, subclass,
-- InventoryType (INVTYPE_ROBE normalized to INVTYPE_CHEST) and Quality bucket with a non-zero
-- DisenchantID, mirroring ItemScaling::KeyOf/BuildCurves/BuildTemplate's disenchantIds curve in
-- src/server/coa/AscensionItemScaling.cpp so newly lifted copies of these items compute the same
-- bracket at runtime. Rows with no eligible donor at or below their ItemLevel in their bucket are
-- left at DisenchantID = 0, unchanged from before this migration.

